# Upstream pins for the vendored native shell.
# Regenerate the baseline and this file with: bin/mob_bridge_diff.sh --refresh
#
# The NDK pin is not cosmetic: bumping it requires rebuilding the OTP tarballs,
# because libbeam.a embeds libc++ symbols under a clang-version-specific inline
# namespace (NDK 27 / clang 18 -> ne180000, NDK 25 / clang 14 -> ne140000).
#
# The zig pin is EXACT and not a floor: MobDev.Toolchain compares the string
# `zig version` prints, so 0.16.0 is refused with the same message a missing
# zig gets. ziglang.org prunes nightlies, so this build is not on the asdf
# plugin's index — it came from the mach mirror (pkg.machengine.org, which
# redirects to pkg.hexops.org) and was unpacked into ~/.asdf/installs/zig by
# hand. See .tool-versions.
#
# mob 0.9.12 with mob_dev 0.7.16 (7 October), which admits `mob ~> 0.9.0`, so
# the override 0.9.3 needed is gone. mob 0.9.8 and later need mob_dev 0.7.7 or
# later (the per-app distribution cookie). mob_new 0.6.3 is still the template:
# what 0.6.4 to 0.6.7 add natively is for deep links (mob 0.9.11), held presses
# on Android (0.9.12) and iPad, none of which Kati uses yet — the Elixir side
# runs on the 0.6.3 shell. `bin/mob_bridge_diff.sh` lists the six files that
# merge would touch.

mob_new=0.6.3
mob=0.9.12
mob_dev=0.7.16
ndk=27.2.12479018
zig=0.17.0-dev.269+ebff43698
erts=17.0
